{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u$", "MATH_0002": "$v$", "MATH_0003": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\colim_\\mathcal{I} M$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$u(\\colim_\\mathcal{I} M) =\n\\colim_\\mathcal{I} u \\circ M$", "MATH_0007": "$u$", "MATH_0008": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\lim_\\mathcal{I} M$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0011": "$v(\\lim_\\mathcal{I} M) =\n\\lim_\\mathcal{I} v \\circ M$", "MATH_0012": "$v$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-adjoint}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoint-exact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:de01b11837e34ed6880602868375f6571e5af43c102377c4267d7dcd9f278960", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d3d0c1838f160dd427ed9ddfcc1a6c5337a7764d95cafc8136e8442fc79a376a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a left adjoint to <MATH_0002> as in Definition <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Suppose that <MATH_0003> is a diagram,\nand suppose that <MATH_0004> exists in\n<MATH_0005>. Then <MATH_0006>. In other words,\n<MATH_0007> commutes with (representable) colimits.\n<STRUCT_0003> Suppose that <MATH_0008> is a diagram,\nand suppose that <MATH_0009> exists in\n<MATH_0010>. Then <MATH_0011>. In other words <MATH_0012> commutes\nwith representable limits.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0a2489f560cd805506983b7c0cbb138f5c8b2ab4ae263803a265e1dfd34693cc", "unit_id": "tag:0038:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(\\colim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i), Y) &\n= & \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(\\colim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i, v(Y)) \\\\\n& = &\n\\lim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}^{opp}}\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(M_i, v(Y)) \\\\\n& = &\n\\lim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}^{opp}}\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(M_i), Y)\n\\end{matrix}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$u(\\colim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-limit-colim}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:546a2043499ca7b0b9fbd81c06469cb66f24374356e89cd80fb0fff78028f04c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:658f0573c56f7a69f2ed82308b47b0d865e5a621916cc64f10cb68017b932ee4", "source_text": "A morphism from a colimit into an object is the same as a compatible\nsystem of morphisms from the constituents of the limit into the\nobject, see Remark <REF_0001>. So\n<MATH_0001>\nproves that <MATH_0002> is\nthe colimit we are looking for.\nA similar argument works for the other statement.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:663c54e40f7aeeb259986a1efdc2ab38634e4d5e43229a803bbeb3e8dce90191", "unit_id": "tag:0038:proof"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u$", "MATH_0002": "$v$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$u$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0006": "$v$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-adjoint}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-exact-adjoint}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9c89cbc4ef5acb3778db7f810618fe07331f3567eb4f88c224c62e91ff0789b9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8cbae6362a1b9e32941384121c1cdcaf654a03db1e0bc938af2fec815f1c0777", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a left adjoint of <MATH_0002> as in Definition <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0003> has finite colimits, then <MATH_0004> is right exact.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> has finite limits, then <MATH_0006> is left exact.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:18e09e285f225cddb7516b607b608075cce4cb5fc546f3068f49008bad65f5ad", "unit_id": "tag:0039:statement"}
